Hardware-Aware Stability Correlation
Embedding the hardware execution profile directly into the analysis pipeline enables cross-run evaluations that answer critical infrastructure questions:
 * Do specific GPU architectures or interconnect fabrics introduce subtle numerical drift in non-linear stress transfer?
 * How do memory bandwidth ceilings on different coprocessors correlate with maximum stable integration timesteps (\Delta t)?
With the multi-node simulation runs, active learning acquisition loops, per-antenna forensic black boxes, and cluster-scale metadata schemas fully mapped, the CMB-0926 framework stands as a complete, self-governing computational physics platform.
